│ Okay, let’s address this issue. The core problem is that Django’s  │
│ parent_link=True in the document_ptr field, combined with          │
│ on_delete=models.CASCADE, is causing issues when dealing with      │
│ multiple OneToOneField references. Specifically, the origin field  │
│ is getting an ImproperlyConfigured error. The issue stems from how │
│ Django handles cascading deletes and the order in which it         │
│ attempts to resolve the parent-child relationships.  The simplest  │
│ and most robust solution is to remove parent_link=True and use     │
│ on_delete=models.PROTECT instead. This will prevent the cascade    │
│ delete from interfering with the OneToOneField relationships and   │
│ resolve the error.                                                 │
