│ Okay, let’s address this issue. The core problem is that Django’s  │
│ parent_link=True in the document_ptr field, combined with          │
│ on_delete=models.CASCADE, is causing issues when dealing with      │
│ multiple OneToOneField references. Specifically, the origin field  │
│ is being flagged as improperly configured because it’s trying to   │
│ reference a parent that might not exist, leading to the            │
│ ImproperlyConfigured error. The issue stems from the fact that     │
│ Django’s ORM doesn’t always handle multiple parent-child           │
│ relationships elegantly when using CASCADE deletion.               │
│                                                                    │
│ The solution is to change the on_delete behavior of the origin     │
│ field to models.PROTECT. This will prevent the deletion of the     │
│ parent document from cascading to the child documents, ensuring    │
│ data integrity. This aligns with the intended behavior of          │
│ preventing orphaned records.                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ Here's the patch:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
